     "field": "definition",
     "severity": "Medium",
     "issue": "The definition misattributes the -14 LUFS figure to AES: 'Following AES streaming recommendations, typical targets are around -14 LUFS.' Web-verified via AES TD1008 (Recommendations for Loudness of Internet Audio Streaming, v3.13) and Production Expert's summary of TD1008: AES actually recommends approx -16 LUFS for music and -18 LUFS for speech, not -14. The -14 LUFS value is a platform loudness-normalization target (Spotify, YouTube, Tidal, Amazon), not an AES recommendation. -1 dBTP is a correct/standard true-peak ceiling.",
     "suggestion": "Attribute -14 LUFS to the streaming platforms rather than AES, e.g. 'Common platform normalization targets are around -14 LUFS integrated (Spotify, YouTube, Tidal) with a maximum true peak of about -1 dBTP; note AES TD1008 itself recommends a quieter target near -16 LUFS.'"
